KG42.register("clusters-e511f57e569df516681ac00d",{"id":"05-double_auction::v142-d-CL009","paper":"05-double_auction","label":"TR marginal trade reduction, payment-receipt differences, and welfare consequences","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL009","label":"TR marginal trade reduction, payment-receipt differences, and welfare consequences","market_meaning":"TR excludes the marginal buyer and seller and restricts the set permitted to trade, using the buyer and seller quotations at the excluded position to determine the payment and receipt rates for permitted traders, respectively. This rate difference may accrue to the operator, and reducing trades also carries the welfare consequences stated in the source text.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M04"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","matching","clearing","pricing","activation","settlement","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"All chains are limited to M04. Excluded marginal participants must be distinguished from actual traders; some C2 interpretations in R020 conflate the two, and the index definition of γ within the same mechanism is not provided in full, so assembly closure is not declared.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Removing the marginal trade and using its quotations to set charges are the set-related, execution, financial, and welfare consequences of the same decision, and the source text explicitly connects these uses. Identical nodes alone are insufficient for assembly; this cluster does not introduce γ or pricing rules from other mechanisms.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R022","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the core textual rule for excluding marginal participants and specifying the number permitted to trade."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R021","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Retains the set expression of the same reduction rule at the execution stage, without treating it as an additional independent exclusion rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R019","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Retains the welfare consequences of the reduction; its numerical limit is another representation of the same reduction rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R023","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Retains the local projection of the overall reduction rule onto buyer participation, without expanding it into a complete set of entry rules."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R024","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides bilateral price inputs determined by marginal quotations."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R025","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Implements the marginal prices as payment and receipt rates for permitted traders."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R020","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Retains the consequence that the rate difference for a single-unit trade may accrue to the operator, while explicitly identifying a conflict in its C2 interpretation of the actors."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL009-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R022","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R021","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The textual matching rule and the execution set expression describe the same marginal reduction; their representational granularity and object declarations differ, and all are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL009-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R022","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R019","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C001","v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly links the exclusion of marginal participants to welfare not being maximized; only this qualitative consequence is recorded, without fabricating a welfare-loss function."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL009-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R022","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R023","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R023::phi::v141-c-R023-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The exclusion of buyer γ from participation is the buyer-side projection of the overall reduction rule for both buyers and sellers and cannot serve as an independent restriction equivalent to the overall rule."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL009-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R022","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R024","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R024::phi::v141-c-R024-C001","v141-c-R024::phi::v141-c-R024-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08","v141-b-g01-ev-06"],"rationale":"After excluding the marginal participants, the source text uses the quotations at their position to specify the rates for permitted traders; this interface does not relist the excluded participants as traders."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL009-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R024","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R025","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R024::theta::v141-c-R024-P001","v141-c-R024::theta::v141-c-R024-P002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R025::theta::v141-c-R025-theta-BgammaP","v141-c-R025::theta::v141-c-R025-theta-SgammaP"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The bilateral marginal prices in the same TR auction enter the buyer's payment and the seller's receipt, respectively, without merging the prices on the two sides."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL009-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R025","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R020","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R025::phi::v141-c-R025-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The difference between the rates paid and received by traders corresponds to the gain attributable to the operator in a single-unit trade; the source's qualification that a gain is possible and its price-ordering conditions are retained."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL009-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R021::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R022::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R022::V::matching.counterparties","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The same TR selection function based on reduction is referenced in the matching, execution, and welfare chains; only the node display is unified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL009-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R024::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R025::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R024::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The same M04 two-sided pricing function appears in price definition and in the application of payments and receipts."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL009-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R020::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R025::V::settlement.payment"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R025::V::settlement.payment","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"The same TR payment and receipt function provides a basis for the use of the operator's spread; the settlement node is not rewritten as a node for a budgetary property."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL009-O04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R020::theta::v141-c-R020-theta-BgammaP","v141-c-R024::theta::v141-c-R024-P001","v141-c-R025::theta::v141-c-R025-theta-BgammaP"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"In the same TR auction, the excluded marginal buyer's bid is used as the rate paid by admitted buyers and as an input to the spread. The mapping is based on parameter meanings and does not endorse the C2 interpretation in R020 that calls the marginal buyer a trader."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL009-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R020::theta::v141-c-R020-theta-SgammaP","v141-c-R024::theta::v141-c-R024-P002","v141-c-R025::theta::v141-c-R025-theta-SgammaP"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"In the same TR auction, the excluded marginal seller's offer is used as the rate received by admitted sellers and as an input to the spread; the local role is retained, and the marginal seller is not identified as a trader."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL009-O06","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C002","v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C001","v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"rationale":"These are the counting, execution-set, and textual versions of the same marginal reduction restriction. Their index declarations, formalization sources, and functional members differ; no substitutable representative is selected at present, and they are not counted again as independent rules."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL009-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The M04 chain uses γ but does not fully provide the ordered index sets and marginal-position definitions for the same mechanism. R019 declares the parameter, R021 explains it only within the expression, and R022 and R023 do not declare the corresponding objects; the missing information cannot be supplied merely on the basis of identical symbols.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022","v141-c-R023","v141-c-R024"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R019::theta::theta_gamma","v141-c-R021::phi::v141-c-R021-C001","v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C001","v141-c-R023::phi::v141-c-R023-C001","v141-c-R024::theta::v141-c-R024-P001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Obtain additional evidence applicable to TR for ordering, indexing, cases with no tradable pairs, and boundary cases, and have C standardize how objects are declared; do not substitute parameters from M02 or M03."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL009-G02","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The parameter meanings in R020 identify both marginal parties as excluded, but its C2 binding explanation also calls them trading buyer γ and trading seller γ, conflicting with the exclusion conditions in R019, R021, R022, and R023.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R020","v141-c-R019","v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022","v141-c-R023"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R020::theta::v141-c-R020-theta-BgammaP","v141-c-R020::theta::v141-c-R020-theta-SgammaP","v141-c-R022::phi::v141-c-R022-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C is to revise the interpretation of the actors to clarify the distinction between the providers of marginal bids and offers and the actual payers and recipients; D is to retain the frozen content and explicitly disclose the conflict."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL009-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The welfare consequences are described only qualitatively, without a calculation of welfare loss; the operator's spread is limited to a single-unit trade and cannot be directly treated as the total gain from a trade involving multiple kWh. Price units, quantity aggregation, and a zero spread at the boundary still require checking.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020","v141-c-R024","v141-c-R025"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C001","v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001","v141-c-R025::phi::v141-c-R025-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If quantitative welfare or total monetary amounts are required, obtain additional evidence for the objectives, units, and traded-volume aggregation relationships of the same mechanism; retain the qualification of possible gains and the single-unit scope, and do not claim that strictly positive gains are guaranteed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL009-G04","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The incentives for truthful bidding and avoidance of subsidies in the source are mechanism properties; the existing selection, settlement, and operator nodes cannot automatically cover full incentive compatibility and budgetary properties.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020","v141-c-R022","v141-c-R025"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R020::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R025::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R022::V::matching.counterparties"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-02","v141-b-g01-prop-03"],"required_work":"Manually process the proposals for property nodes that remain unapproved; if coverage needs to be extended, C is to add source-supported property rules. Do not infer incentives for truthfulness from reduction or the spread alone."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL009-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence for TR prices, reduction, welfare, and operator gains is UNREVIEWED; this cluster has undergone neither independent source review nor scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020","v141-c-R021","v141-c-R022","v141-c-R023","v141-c-R024","v141-c-R025"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-06","v141-b-g01-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently check the TR passages, tables, and index explanations before examining the existing formalization."}]},"rule_refs":["05-double_auction::v141-c-R022","05-double_auction::v141-c-R021","05-double_auction::v141-c-R019","05-double_auction::v141-c-R023","05-double_auction::v141-c-R024","05-double_auction::v141-c-R025","05-double_auction::v141-c-R020"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-67068978718ed583","COMP-72f84a438787fbd5","COMP-abf87986b4b368b7","COMP-c93e24704bedd55e","COMP-d4d038c21a480e0b"]});
